# Wave W17-U (Route 202): gate turf — approach meadow, bed-flecked: a kept green carrying pale petal flecks drifted off the city beds that thicken toward Revelry (design: the towers appear before the road feels long; the shipped flower beds stand byte-preserved as the route’s dressing and the ground converts around them). Route 202’s own ground — split from Route 201’s shore meadow by the petals themselves (city beds vs lake shore) and from Route 117’s field green (Maris) by register: this meadow is a city’s front garden, not a farm’s field.
